    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8aa420e3_7e91cac8",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 10,
      "author": {
        "id": 1945845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-27T04:00:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I pretty strongly disagree. The kernel/bootloader interface should really stay stable so we don\u0027t tightly tie kernel version functionality to bootloader versions. \n\nEspecially as multiple vendors are using this interface.\n\nHaving multiple version support in the kernel allows kernels to be tested and updated on devices without requiring the bootloader also be updated. It also allows for new features to be added to KABI frozen kernels without breaking things.",
      "parentUuid": "f1bc5a62_a2d3c1d4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
        "startChar": 54,
        "endLine": 10,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "38f32cbb2220e7a9274e1e40b28dc0367db9f003",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "827d97f8_9915b6a7",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 10,
      "author": {
        "id": 1334815
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-27T04:18:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If kallsyms feature is removed or module memory feature is also changed one day, part of old debug_kinfo items must be refactored(removed or added). And then how to maintain this CL ?\n  ex. android kernel 6.1 upgraded to 6.6, we have debug_kinfo changes to delete some old members and add new members (see https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common.git/+/ac3b43283923440900b4f36ca5f9f0b1ca43b70e or b/330221056#comment5) ?\n\nVendor or pixel kernel can create the other local kinfo to backup their new items directly, like pixel_debug_kinfo.c instead of debug_kinfo in aosp.",
      "parentUuid": "8aa420e3_7e91cac8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
        "startChar": 54,
        "endLine": 10,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "38f32cbb2220e7a9274e1e40b28dc0367db9f003",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "81caf506_b08ac666",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 10,
      "author": {
        "id": 1945845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-27T04:41:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When additions or deletions need to be made, we should change the interface version. It may not be possible for every kernel to support every interface version, but an effort should be made to keep things compatible so we don\u0027t needlessly tie kernel and bootloader versions, especially just loosely based on the kernel branch.\n\nMy understanding is there are also limits to what vendors can do with kinfo on their own as some symbols are intentionally not exported to vendor modules.",
      "parentUuid": "827d97f8_9915b6a7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
        "startChar": 54,
        "endLine": 10,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "38f32cbb2220e7a9274e1e40b28dc0367db9f003",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
