      "writtenOn": "2024-09-30T05:22:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unlike before, I heard that not only platform but also kernel update is going on in one device. (It is necessary to change the bootloader whenever the structure of debug_kinfo is updated.) Therefore, in order to preserve the current debug_kinfo as much as possible, we tried to divided version.\nHowever, as you said, if there is a value that needs to be changed among the existing values, the bootloader need to be modified.\n\nWhen I first created issue tracker, I tried to add _seqs_of_names_pa value. Then, because of the stability of debug_kinfo, we divided the version. (I have also written a patch that puts _seqs_of_names without dividing the version https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/kernel/common/+/3172239 )\nShould I just add the _seqs_of_names_pa value in the same way as before? Or do we need to discuss more about debug_kinfo? @jstultz@google.com @jonechou@google.com",
      "parentUuid": "1110522d_7eae534c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
        "startChar": 54,
        "endLine": 10,
        "endChar": 35
      },
